HTMLCut core includes selector bindings and serialization portions adapted from
rust-scraper. Those portions retain their ISC terms and copyright attribution in
LICENSE-ISC. Original HTMLCut source retains MPL-2.0 terms in LICENSE. The package
license expression requires both applicable sets of terms. Parsing and matching
use maintained html5ever and selectors crates through a private admitted DOM.
Upstream source: https://github.com/rust-scraper/scraper
HTMLCut source and modifications: https://github.com/resoltico/HTMLCut
